      "narratorTurn": 1,
      "tokenCount": 1038,
      "content": "I am Nera Veyrath, the eleven-year-old third child of Duke Cassian Veyrath and the late Ilyra Veyrath.\n\nUntil today, this body belonged to the original Nera Veyrath: a noble child who had already begun growing into someone cruel, spoiled, and feared by the people beneath him. He had struck servants, threatened wages, humiliated commoners, and learned that his family name usually protected him from consequences.\n\nBut this morning, on 18 September 731, I awakened as Nera with memories of another life and memories of a game called *Asterfall: Crowns of the Last Dawn*.\n\nI know this world.\n\nOr at least, I know versions of what it might become.\n\nI remember major characters, public events, conflicts, wars, deaths, and endings from the game. I remember that Nera Veyrath was supposed to become one of its antagonistic figures. I remember Crownspire Imperial Academy, which I am supposed to enter at eighteen. I remember people who may someday become allies, rivals, enemies, or something more.\n\nBut I do not remember everything.\n\nI don't know every private conversation, hidden motive, secret meeting, or exact event. The game skipped most of Nera's childhood, so the seven years between now and Crownspire are especially uncertain to me. Different routes contradicted each other, and what I remember is not destiny. If events change, then the future I remember may change with them.\n\nThe people around me are real people now, not characters following a script.\n\nMy mother, Ilyra Veyrath, is already dead.\n\nShe died six weeks after transferring Isolde Veyless's soul bond to me. I remember loving my mother before her death. Whatever the original Nera became afterward, that loss was real.\n\nIsolde has remained beside me since then.\n\nShe is permanently soul-bound to serve and protect me. The bond cannot simply be removed, and I cannot transfer it away. It can compel service and prevent her from deliberately harming me, but it cannot create affection, trust, loyalty beyond its requirements, or genuine emotion.\n\nAt this point in her life, Isolde's reassuring expressions are largely learned performances. I should not assume that obedience means she likes me.\n\nI also remember fragments of what the original Nera has already done.\n\nOne of them concerns Alaric Dawnmere.\n\nDuring a hunting journey when Nera was ten, his entourage forced Alaric's family grain cart from the road. When they resisted, Nera ordered punishment. Alaric saw his father suffer an injury that permanently damaged his working arm.\n\nThat has already happened.\n\nWhatever I choose from this point forward cannot erase it.\n\nToday, however, another event is unfolding—one I remember differently from the original history.\n\nA fire broke out in my mother's locked rooms.\n\nLiora Fen, an eleven-year-old servant's daughter who once played with Nera when they were younger, stole her mother Elise's keys and entered the rooms. She was trying to retrieve and repair my mother's silver mechanical nightingale. While attempting to use an aether warming lamp, she accidentally knocked it into the curtains.\n\nThe fire damaged my mother's rooms.\n\nPart of Ilyra's final portrait was burned.\n\nLiora burned her palm. Elise burned her forearm while getting her daughter out and helping extinguish the fire.\n\nBoth survived.\n\nIn the history I remember from the game, this incident became something much worse. Elise died, Liora was left without her mother, and that loss helped shape the person Liora later became.\n\nBut that future has not happened yet.\n\nRight now Elise is alive.\n\nLiora is alive.\n\nNeither has been tortured.\n\nAnd I have not decided what happens to either of them.\n\nThere is another problem.\n\nBastian Krail, one of House Veyrath's senior household officials, claims that a shipping folio disappeared during the fire. He has connected its disappearance to Elise's responsibility for the keys and Liora's unauthorized entry into the room.\n\nI do not know whether his accusation is true.\n\nMy memories of the game do not give me reliable knowledge of what happened to that folio.\n\nI know only what Nera himself currently knows, what I personally remember, and whatever I can discover from this point forward.\n\nThe hearing is taking place in the west reception room of the Veyrath estate.\n\nElise and Liora have been brought before me.\n\nBastian Krail has prepared a punishment order and is waiting for my approval.\n\nIsolde is beside me.\n\nMy mother's damaged portrait is nearby.\n\nMagerrett Veyrath is somewhere outside the room, close enough to listen, while Taigar Veyrath is farther down the corridor.\n\nThe punishment order has not been signed.\n\nNo judgment has been made.\n\nNo punishment has been authorized.\n\nThis is where my story begins.",
      "order": 1,
      "role": "user",
